There are many tools that can interact with an Android application running inside your Android 11 virtual phone. They operate at different levels: some control the phone, some interact with the screen, others inspect application code, monitor runtime behaviour, or communicate with the application's APIs.

Here is a comprehensive toolkit for mobile application security research.

### 1\. Tools that directly interact with the virtual phone

Device control, installation, screen interaction and debugging

![](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/s7dMBKaKa1AN_TK4E3XrBzk6fZWHGQegA-3Hk3OZpwQSSDYBmnU0Mf-S3Zs-8H7fhMfzPoi6xl_ZfTZuLTOTr_LpF9ozEW1NDgsVHPZ3aa7J0IxNYXpC6EbEJUIFlVlzfbPnl2PNTVC0zzQO75UYxKSjBWN7WWPtDCugz8wC6b3-9bjLfYurOeecKU_pQbc6?purpose=fullsize)

1\. ADB

Controls the Android emulator from Ubuntu.

* Install and uninstall applications.

* Launch applications.

* Execute Android shell commands.

* Read logs.

* Transfer files.

* Take screenshots.

* Inspect packages.

```bash
adb devices
adb shell
adb install app.apk
adb logcat
```

![Can I have the Android Emulator without the Window Frame? - Stack Overflow](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/k1iyRDbk1OV7tcapjgS1SL_4JhXPrFeN0Rb7JLpHKSjiKd-__KYsMiDCoubBErQBcW9RHBbJRWy6HIpb47uaiPs-CzkJlwA82R4axMzCGEwuOzBGqP3suLhhrac5TFpGzf_1swKkpCDQ6xmFk3hYt-3mKmNbn8e-Qbv3wX96mNRg1up97qT8WUwKsc0i3kfJ?purpose=fullsize)

2\. Android Studio

* Launch and manage virtual phones.

* Inspect application layouts.

* Debug applications.

* Monitor CPU and memory.

* Inspect application processes.

[Official website](https://developer.android.com/studio?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

