### 2\. Tools that interact with application code at runtime

These are especially useful for offensive security research in an authorised laboratory.

![Dynamic Instrumentation on Linux/Android using Frida](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/sn1M8bhunnGfyhGd6uAurGuPvxmiSQlvW0y4TbyIZUIuFF5PJlhPO90XwtJWM_WNu19ZT3zBptomm2GqACq00E_qgTPb7R51B039RuhOurzjC6Rfvxr5EVRQP-GdwnXRNPffd3LiAe4tylqq7viPJ2mdg9o2x8BegEOH_AJoPUGhlp6BFgdiX-jfZSf2Essb?purpose=fullsize)

6\. Frida

Observe and instrument application methods while the app is running.

* Observe method calls.

* Inspect runtime values.

* Trace application behaviour.

* Investigate cryptographic functions.

* Understand application execution.

[Official website](https://frida.re/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

![Objection 2026: Runtime Mobile App Exploration with Frida (Commands & Setup)](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/k-9zpRxOePOxNYn2anvRb1NarKEn4M_U6hrJmEVv8nHG_fAWsVS5tSWoYzoQMim6gOAjFF6tm5rYwoM2zl5ovjPOG9dXeQBB4X75iLVMGQubR8dNncaSu2S6hbEVAiR5eavHeshjtoET06EBJdWn3q1wuKrvUSGYliCLYw1MTi9PjsN483_dhUV8XsLhuUYg?purpose=fullsize)

7\. Objection

A runtime exploration tool built around Frida.

* Explore application environments.

* Inspect files and preferences.

* Examine runtime properties.

* Investigate Android security configurations.

[Official project](https://github.com/sensepost/objection?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

![Debug dell'app  |  Android Studio  |  Android Developers](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/2kbegGCHnh_taFGh5nA-ofK0HGZBysusd5dGWCvjA45g9B83WMI21NECpAQ2Pvek_aBi5hWIagpneLfQt0idoFK6dKuhfX8EbE8mSrpPJ3hq9Vq6ZCRqlsP72y2vcn7fnuuQkMfDmeYNiD0Z-B-MFwwj51Hf3A4caOjfHaCiN6hbgba92e6PCb2Bx_ztPFlc?purpose=fullsize)

8\. LLDB

Debug native Android application code.

* Inspect native processes.

* Examine memory and variables.

* Set breakpoints.

* Investigate native libraries.

![Use the debugger in Android Studio  |  Android Developers](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/e0uKkHU9rQl4HGhAv_zF6zOxqCRj8NpbqMs_ueLX0QAHmoKIzv1EiNjsrWmNoJbI09yYl4vZxs6C7ZqTt2EjPOXQsNDkHeqB300k1e5uxc3PoAJ6yUFOl-3c8urFYovYMVsrKtOrZb0KOLVIA_RbSvhbDnC3aa78fO-HSFGjQVzk4q4fQZZp1O8WArqNdxhN?purpose=fullsize)

9\. JDWP

Supports debugging compatible Android Java applications.

* Inspect execution.

* Set breakpoints.

* Examine variables.

* Follow method execution.

Access depends on application debugging configuration.

### 3\. Tools that inspect and analyse APK files

These tools interact with the application's package and code, rather than necessarily controlling its screen.

| Tool            | Main function                               |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| JADX            | Decompile APKs into readable Java-like code |
| APKTool         | Decode resources and Smali                  |
| MobSF           | Automated mobile security analysis          |
| Androguard      | Programmatic APK analysis                   |
| Ghidra          | Reverse-engineer native libraries           |
| Bytecode Viewer | Inspect compiled application code           |
| Apk Analyzer    | Inspect APK structure and contents          |

### 4\. Tools that inspect application network communication

These tools help you investigate what the application sends and receives.

![](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/-aL2WRXuR2ijlvtWrqYZN1DDGPB3Rc9KhxWu3DNcL0IwvnsERoVHcYfbpzvYwofKuSmsHw_zZY4lmPu7KlYHwDMhLSzYue4seNVk4vkkXp9T2OtK2P-Ngu2qLFogUAkwGncrZ7OZuvneb3lopSSDuG2IVCuDiwgECJvwzGBxZJsSrGi9UIfk1z3q3nAMWif9?purpose=fullsize)

10\. Wireshark

Captures and analyses network packets.

* DNS

* TCP

* UDP

* TLS

* HTTP traffic when visible

    [Website](https://www.wireshark.org/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

